    "slug": "caged-the-complete-window",
    "title": "Every Note in the Window",
    "summary": "The five CAGED windows now hold every degree of the major scale, and none of it needs memorising dot by dot: the roots you already know, plus one rule — a 4 above every 3, a 7 below every 1 — regenerates the rest.",
    "tags": ["caged", "fretboard"],
    "readingTimeMin": 4,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-11"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        { "text": "Five windows, and now each one holds all seven degrees of " },
        { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": " major — nothing left to add. That's the promise chapter 1 made, closed: five shapes, learned once, filled in four times over four chapters, and you were never handed a sixth. With the D form finished, the C, A, G, E and D forms you already know are all complete."
        }
      ]
    },
